        "original_id": "f928b914-d9c1-5b2e-ab98-64ebf0eb9aa2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Howea forsteriana, Howea species, Bulbophyllum\n- Places: Northern Hemisphere, Lord Howe Island, Africa, southern Asia, Latin America, West Indies, Indian Ocean islands, Pacific Ocean islands\n- Industries: Palm seed industry, seedling trade\n\nFacts:\n- Howea forsteriana is commonly grown as an indoor plant in the Northern Hemisphere.\n- The two Howea species form the mainstay of Lord Howe Island's palm seed industry.\n- The two Howea species are even more important to Lord Howe Island's trade in newly germinated seedlings.\n- Bulbophyllum is found throughout most warm parts of the world, including Africa, southern Asia, Latin America, the West Indies, and islands in the Indian and Pacific Oceans.",
